        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(ios): preserve localized settings accessibility labels",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes the current main CI failure in `test/scripts/apple-app-i18n.test.ts`. The Apple i18n guard rejects `LocalizedStringKey` wrapper helpers when their accessibility labels bypass the `Text(...)` localized lookup path.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nTwo settings helpers accept `LocalizedStringKey` titles but passed the key directly to `.accessibilityLabel(title)`. Wrapping those labels with `Text(title)` matches the existing i18n wrapper contract and keeps accessibility strings on the localized SwiftUI text path.\n\n## User Impact\n\nSettings rows keep localized accessibility labels, and unrelated PRs are no longer blocked by the Apple i18n guard failure on main.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kxckw4grcgamhgje275xpcp3`: `corepack pnpm test test/scripts/apple-app-i18n.test.ts` — 13 tests passed.\n- Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kxckw4grcgamhgje275xpcp3`: `OPENCLAW_CHECK_CHANGED_REMOTE_CHILD=1 OPENCLAW_CHANGED_LANES_RAW_SYNC=1 corepack pnpm check:changed` — passed.\n- Autoreview: clean, no accepted/actionable findings.\n- `git diff --check` — passed.\n",
